  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41301" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening household resilience and livelihoods and enhancing food security and nutrition among the most vulnerable households in the context of  2022 economic and food crisis in Sri Lanka</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To develop 2500 Home Gardens targeting households which have one or more cases of severely malnourished children (-3 SD children between 0-5 years with a less than -3 standard deviation of weight for height.
To provide training to the care givers of these identified 2500 households to improve family dietary habits for better nutrition, including the use of healthy recipes developed using nutritious foods available locally.
To provide locally available nutritious food ingredients (five-grain flour mixture) to supplement diets of these severely malnourished children. The supplemented food will compensate for the household cash shortfall, that would ideally be spent on food and nutritional requirements</narrative>
  </description>
